# Check text out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which gives a CRLF (or mixed) working tree that differs
# byte-for-byte from what's committed and deployed — anything that hashes or
# compares exact file content (CSP hashes for inline scripts, generated-output
# checks) then disagrees between a Windows machine and CI/production.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
